<!-- DataTables library tags. Shared by datatables.ejs (results/fixture tables) and
     datatables-stats.ejs (stats tables) so the URLs are declared in one place.
     Six views each carried their own copy, and they had drifted: three asked for a
     bundle with b-html5 (the CSV button) and three for one without, so the browser
     fetched two different 200KB+ bundles across a session.

     Note the bundle has no jQuery in it (no `jq-` segment in its builder URL). It used
     to include jQuery 3.3.1, which was fetched on top of the copy footer.ejs already
     self-hosts from node_modules, then replaced window.jQuery with a second instance
     that carries none of the Bootstrap plugins registered on the first.

     Self-hosted since HARD-45, in static/vendor/datatables/. They are byte-for-byte
     what cdn.datatables.net served, not an npm install: the bundle is a builder output
     (DataTables 1.10.20, Buttons 1.6.1, ColVis, HTML5 export, FixedHeader 3.1.6,
     Responsive 2.2.3 - the rebuild link is in its header) and the npm equivalent is ten
     packages at different versions, which is an upgrade, not a move. The two plug-ins
     are date-euro (plug-ins 1.10.19) and page.jumpToData() (1.12.0).

     `defer` keeps document order, so the plug-ins still run after the bundle they
     register on, and all of it before DOMContentLoaded - which is when jQuery's ready
     fires the inline initialisers in datatables.ejs and datatables-stats.ejs. -->
<script defer src="<%= asset('/static/vendor/datatables/datatables.min.js') %>"></script>
<script defer src="<%= asset('/static/vendor/datatables/date-euro.js') %>"></script>
<script defer src="<%= asset('/static/vendor/datatables/page.jumpToData.js') %>"></script>
